 "lines": {
  "hook": "Your boat is gone, and you're alone in a raft.",
  "b1": "One sailor lived through exactly this, so guess how many days he lasted.",
  "b2": "Seventy six days, in a raft about six feet long.",
  "b3": "He distilled drinking water and caught fish.",
  "b4": "Survival trainers say every drop of body water you save buys you time.",
  "b5": "So put up the canopy, save your energy, and ration your sweat.",
  "b6": "Stream the sea anchor to stay near your last reported position.",
  "b7": "Switch on your emergency beacon and leave it on.",
  "b8": "Keep flashing a mirror at the horizon.",
  "end": "Seventy six days, and it started just like this, alone in a raft."
 },
